1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,268
The iPhone 18 Pro is finally here

2
00:00:02,268 --> 00:00:03,837
It has speed may surprise you

3
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:05,538
a smaller Dynamic Island

4
00:00:05,538 --> 00:00:06,439
faster charging

5
00:00:06,439 --> 00:00:08,008
and a variable aperture

6
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:10,744
So is this variable aperture actually useful

7
00:00:10,744 --> 00:00:12,679
How much faster is A20 Pro

8
00:00:12,679 --> 00:00:15,081
And what other surprises this phone has? 

9
00:00:15,081 --> 00:00:16,349
Let's talk about it

10
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:17,283
in one take

11
00:00:41,341 --> 00:00:41,875
First

12
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:42,642
design

13
00:00:42,642 --> 00:00:44,644
the iPhone 18 Pro haven't changed much

14
00:00:44,644 --> 00:00:45,412
They keep the metal and-glass design

15
00:00:45,412 --> 00:00:47,080
from last year

16
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:47,981
but the color difference

17
00:00:47,981 --> 00:00:50,150
between two materials is less now

18
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:50,517
Still

19
00:00:50,517 --> 00:00:51,785
the uneven seam issues

20
00:00:51,785 --> 00:00:54,087
from the 17 Pro aren't really fixed

21
00:00:54,087 --> 00:00:54,854
For colors

22
00:00:54,854 --> 00:00:56,823
beyond classic Silver and Black

23
00:00:56,823 --> 00:00:58,324
there’s Glacier Blue

24
00:00:58,324 --> 00:01:00,727
kind of like the 13 Pro’s Sierra Blue

25
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:03,196
But the hero color is definitely Burgundy

26
00:01:03,196 --> 00:01:04,964
It’s got a dark purple undertone

27
00:01:04,964 --> 00:01:06,666
and looks just like red wine

28
00:01:06,666 --> 00:01:08,401
not recommended for minors

29
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:09,302
Around the sides

30
00:01:09,302 --> 00:01:10,904
thickness is unchanged

31
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:12,939
but the camera bump is even thicker

32
00:01:12,939 --> 00:01:15,675
The 18 Pro Max is now 249g

33
00:01:15,675 --> 00:01:17,010
heavist iPhone Ever

34
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:19,879
The Pro is up to 211g too

35
00:01:19,879 --> 00:01:22,348
which is pretty heavy for a 6.3-inch phone

36
00:01:22,348 --> 00:01:23,850
But the most interesting thing

37
00:01:23,850 --> 00:01:25,452
is the new Dynamic Island

38
00:01:25,452 --> 00:01:26,820
How did they shrink it?

39
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:27,720
On older iPhones

40
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:30,023
the Dynamic Island housed a illuminator

41
00:01:30,023 --> 00:01:31,024
a dot projector

42
00:01:31,024 --> 00:01:32,025
an infrared camera

43
00:01:32,025 --> 00:01:32,959
and a front camera

44
00:01:32,959 --> 00:01:33,793
When you unlock

45
00:01:33,793 --> 00:01:36,663
the dot projector casts thousands of dots onto it

46
00:01:36,663 --> 00:01:38,631
The infrared camera reads those dots

47
00:01:38,631 --> 00:01:40,066
checks it against saved data

48
00:01:40,066 --> 00:01:41,034
and unlock

49
00:01:41,034 --> 00:01:42,268
But on the iPhone 18 Pro

50
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:44,571
the infrared camera now sits under the screen

51
00:01:44,571 --> 00:01:46,306
If we look through a microscope

52
00:01:46,306 --> 00:01:48,741
this is how the screen’s pixels normally line up

53
00:01:48,741 --> 00:01:51,478
but this area has about half as many pixels

54
00:01:51,478 --> 00:01:53,446
so the camera underneath can see through

55
00:01:53,446 --> 00:01:55,849
Apple also made the pixels over the camera brighter

56
00:01:55,849 --> 00:01:57,383
and slowly packed the pixels

57
00:01:57,383 --> 00:01:59,085
closer together toward the edges

58
00:01:59,085 --> 00:02:00,887
until they match the rest of the screen

59
00:02:00,887 --> 00:02:02,455
so at a normal viewing distance

60
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:04,157
this area blends in pretty well

61
00:02:04,157 --> 00:02:05,225
As for the unlock speed

62
00:02:05,225 --> 00:02:06,860
it’s about the same as before

63
00:02:07,327 --> 00:02:08,094
So what do we gain

64
00:02:08,094 --> 00:02:09,162
from the smaller cutout?

65
00:02:09,162 --> 00:02:09,963
As you can see

66
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:12,298
the Dynamic Island now has a whopping...

67
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:14,234
130 more pixels

68
00:02:14,234 --> 00:02:15,935
You can squeeze in one more icon

69
00:02:15,935 --> 00:02:17,937
to show three live activities

70
00:02:17,937 --> 00:02:18,972
Most importantly

71
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:20,273
when you post a screenshot

72
00:02:20,273 --> 00:02:21,074
Your friends can tell

73
00:02:21,074 --> 00:02:22,675
you changed to the new iPhone

74
00:02:22,675 --> 00:02:23,977
Beyond the Dynamic Island

75
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:25,411
the screen hasn’t changed much

76
00:02:25,411 --> 00:02:26,880
with full-screen brightness still

77
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:28,281
at just over 1000 nits

78
00:02:28,281 --> 00:02:29,749
the same as before

79
00:02:29,749 --> 00:02:31,384
So what about the cameras?

80
00:02:31,384 --> 00:02:32,919
The biggest camera upgrade this year

81
00:02:32,919 --> 00:02:34,287
is this variable aperture

82
00:02:34,287 --> 00:02:37,323
which can go from F4 to F1.48

83
00:02:37,657 --> 00:02:39,425
So what are the benefits

84
00:02:39,425 --> 00:02:40,193
For example

85
00:02:40,293 --> 00:02:41,895
there’s an alpaca right behind me

86
00:02:41,895 --> 00:02:43,696
If the camera focuses on my face

87
00:02:43,696 --> 00:02:45,031
his face looks blurry

88
00:02:45,031 --> 00:02:46,933
But if the camera focuses on his face

89
00:02:46,933 --> 00:02:48,401
my face gets blurry

90
00:02:48,401 --> 00:02:49,068
That’s because

91
00:02:49,068 --> 00:02:50,937
with a fixed camera settings

92
00:02:50,937 --> 00:02:52,839
only a limited range can look sharp

93
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:55,108
This range is called depth of field

94
00:02:55,108 --> 00:02:57,410
We’re too far to fall within that range

95
00:02:57,410 --> 00:02:58,478
So, how do we fix it?

96
00:03:02,115 --> 00:03:03,449
I tried calling him over

97
00:03:03,449 --> 00:03:04,517
but he won’t come

98
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:08,321
So we can also change the camera’s aperture from f/1.4 to f/5.6

99
00:03:08,321 --> 00:03:10,256
So the blurry spots are smaller

100
00:03:10,256 --> 00:03:12,125
and both our faces are sharper

101
00:03:12,225 --> 00:03:14,327
But there’s also a downside to this

102
00:03:14,327 --> 00:03:16,095
As those blurry spots get smaller

103
00:03:16,095 --> 00:03:18,298
we lose this beautiful background blur

104
00:03:18,298 --> 00:03:19,365
So when filming

105
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:21,067
if you want to shoot a big scene 

106
00:03:21,067 --> 00:03:22,569
and allowing see everything

107
00:03:22,569 --> 00:03:23,870
we got to use a small aperture

108
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:27,340
If you want to bring out someone’s feelings and create a dreamy mood

109
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:28,808
use a large aperture

110
00:03:28,808 --> 00:03:29,642
But in practice

111
00:03:29,642 --> 00:03:32,879
depth of field changes little from wide open to F4

112
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:34,681
take a look at these sample shots

113
00:03:45,258 --> 00:03:46,025
You may have noticed

114
00:03:46,025 --> 00:03:47,227
in those sample shots

115
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,262
the background lights looked like stars

116
00:03:49,262 --> 00:03:51,364
That is because with a smaller aperture

117
00:03:51,364 --> 00:03:53,366
light bends more around the blade edges

118
00:03:53,533 --> 00:03:54,734
turning point of light

119
00:03:54,834 --> 00:03:55,868
into bright rays

120
00:03:56,035 --> 00:03:57,236
With this year’s iPhone

121
00:03:57,236 --> 00:03:58,871
in scenes full of lights like this

122
00:03:58,871 --> 00:04:00,873
just close down to F1.8

123
00:04:00,873 --> 00:04:02,408
to get these star shapes

124
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:04,777
At F4, the stars stand out more

125
00:04:04,777 --> 00:04:06,045
Do you guys like this look

126
00:04:09,549 --> 00:04:10,617
If you like this look

127
00:04:10,617 --> 00:04:13,620
this 10 dollar star filter will have the same effect

128
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:14,420
With those tricks

129
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,189
we change how a photo looks

130
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:17,223
But in videos

131
00:04:17,223 --> 00:04:20,293
aperture also effect how motion feels

132
00:04:20,293 --> 00:04:21,861
When we shoot video in bright light

133
00:04:21,861 --> 00:04:23,997
iPhone raises the shutter speed

134
00:04:23,997 --> 00:04:24,764
to let in less light

135
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:27,467
but that makes moving objects look very choppy

136
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,469
So now you can get the aperture smaller

137
00:04:29,469 --> 00:04:31,237
and bring shutter speed back to normal

138
00:04:31,638 --> 00:04:33,740
that'll make movement feel natural again

139
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:38,411
But in order to use shutter speed and aperture like this

140
00:04:38,411 --> 00:04:40,246
you'd manually control them

141
00:04:40,246 --> 00:04:42,115
That’s where the 18 Pro’s new feature comes in:

142
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,049
Pro Controls

143
00:04:43,049 --> 00:04:44,484
you can now set shutter speed

144
00:04:44,484 --> 00:04:45,151
aperture

145
00:04:45,151 --> 00:04:46,886
focus, and white balance

146
00:04:46,919 --> 00:04:49,355
and use a histogram to check exposure

147
00:04:49,355 --> 00:04:52,292
It brings in lots of features from third-party apps

148
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,893
and it’s really handy

149
00:04:53,993 --> 00:04:54,627
Sadly

150
00:04:54,627 --> 00:04:56,863
this feature is only on 18 Pro

151
00:04:56,863 --> 00:04:57,430
Also

152
00:04:57,430 --> 00:04:59,065
the aperture can adjust itself

153
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:00,366
when you're shooting at a document

154
00:05:00,366 --> 00:05:01,134
it gets smaller

155
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:02,602
to get sharper details

156
00:05:02,602 --> 00:05:04,671
when there a point of light in the frame

157
00:05:04,671 --> 00:05:05,638
it gets bigger

158
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:06,506
to reduce flare

159
00:05:06,539 --> 00:05:09,242
which brings us to this year’s iPhone's major problem 

160
00:05:09,242 --> 00:05:10,109
After the event

161
00:05:10,109 --> 00:05:12,445
Apple organized some test shoots for press

162
00:05:12,712 --> 00:05:14,781
including a scene that looked like a bar

163
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:16,215
While shooting, I was like

164
00:05:16,215 --> 00:05:17,984
why is the lens flare so bad?

165
00:05:18,284 --> 00:05:19,018
So once we got back

166
00:05:19,018 --> 00:05:19,252
So once we got back

167
00:05:19,252 --> 00:05:20,787
We took some quick test

168
00:05:21,287 --> 00:05:23,289
Wide open at F1.48

169
00:05:23,289 --> 00:05:24,924
as we increase light's angle

170
00:05:24,924 --> 00:05:27,260
a curved streak of flare appears

171
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:28,494
on iPhone 18 Pro

172
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:30,530
At the smallest aperture, F4

173
00:05:30,530 --> 00:05:32,432
that curve flare is still there

174
00:05:32,432 --> 00:05:34,467
with petal-shaped spots around the light

175
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:37,170
Flare is pretty noticeable on this year's iPhone

176
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:40,506
So we also test it against the 17 Pro on location

177
00:05:40,907 --> 00:05:43,076
We set the aperture to F1.8

178
00:05:43,076 --> 00:05:44,711
close to the 17 Pro

179
00:05:44,711 --> 00:05:45,945
and at the same light angle

180
00:05:45,945 --> 00:05:48,481
the 17 Pro also shows flare

181
00:05:48,481 --> 00:05:50,383
but over all it looks less severe 

182
00:05:50,616 --> 00:05:52,418
So how does flare affect your shots?

183
00:05:52,418 --> 00:05:54,087
It makes the image look washed out

184
00:05:54,087 --> 00:05:55,154
lowers contrast

185
00:05:55,154 --> 00:05:57,557
and those petal-shaped spots at smaller apertures 

186
00:05:57,557 --> 00:05:59,158
can really spoil the shot

187
00:05:59,158 --> 00:06:00,760
So how can we fix it?

188
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:01,327
First

189
00:06:01,327 --> 00:06:03,096
avoid shooting in bright light

190
00:06:03,096 --> 00:06:03,863
And second

191
00:06:03,863 --> 00:06:05,698
We 3D-printed a lens hood

192
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:06,466
With it on

193
00:06:06,466 --> 00:06:08,835
the flare is reduced to some degree

194
00:06:08,835 --> 00:06:11,604
and we’ve uploaded the 3D model to MakerWorld

195
00:06:12,472 --> 00:06:14,774
the 18 Pro gets Photographic Styles 3

196
00:06:14,807 --> 00:06:17,276
adds new controls for texture and grain

197
00:06:17,276 --> 00:06:18,845
it can make your photo look better

198
00:06:18,845 --> 00:06:20,947
This film effect adds a layer of grain

199
00:06:20,947 --> 00:06:22,715
plus a red glow around bright lights

200
00:06:22,815 --> 00:06:24,417
giving it a pretty nice film look

201
00:06:24,417 --> 00:06:27,320
The most useful feature has to be skin smoothing

202
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:29,222
It smooths skin very naturally

203
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:30,323
keeping its texture

204
00:06:30,323 --> 00:06:32,024
so it still looks pretty real

205
00:06:32,024 --> 00:06:33,593
now that the iPhone’s all grown up

206
00:06:33,593 --> 00:06:35,561
its image quality is really good

207
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:38,898
But better image quality doesn’t always mean a better shot

208
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:41,901
A lot of people actually love the retro look of the old phones

209
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:44,804
So we took the same video with 18 Pro and iPhone 5

210
00:06:45,138 --> 00:06:46,606
Which one do you like more?

211
00:06:46,606 --> 00:06:47,874
Tell us in the comments

212
00:07:24,844 --> 00:07:26,179
Now let's talk about the signal

213
00:07:26,179 --> 00:07:28,681
the 18 Pro uses Apple's own C2 modem

214
00:07:28,681 --> 00:07:30,550
it handles your mobile data

215
00:07:30,550 --> 00:07:32,685
it's Apple's first modem to the Pro iPhone

216
00:07:32,685 --> 00:07:34,020
so is it better than Qualcomm

217
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:34,353
so is it better than Qualcomm

218
00:07:34,353 --> 00:07:37,256
we tested it against the 17 Pro

219
00:07:37,256 --> 00:07:39,859
with a strong 5G signal averaging 10 speed tests

220
00:07:39,992 --> 00:07:41,928
the 18 Pro's download was nearly

221
00:07:41,928 --> 00:07:43,996
20 Mbps slower than the 17 Pro's

222
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,032
uploads was 30 Mbps slower

223
00:07:46,032 --> 00:07:48,434
and latency was 1.4 ms higher

224
00:07:48,534 --> 00:07:51,070
so Apple's modem still seem a bit behind Qualcomm's

225
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:53,439
But in an underground garage with a weaker signal

226
00:07:53,673 --> 00:07:56,409
the 18 Pro came out ahead beating last year's model in

227
00:07:56,409 --> 00:07:59,779
both download and upload speeds with latency also lower

228
00:07:59,846 --> 00:08:02,381
so Apple's own modem may handle weak signals better

229
00:08:02,615 --> 00:08:04,050
We also tried making calls in an

230
00:08:04,050 --> 00:08:05,685
elevator with very poor signal

231
00:08:05,685 --> 00:08:06,853
and both the iPhone 18 Pro

232
00:08:06,853 --> 00:08:08,254
and 17 Pro could connect

233
00:08:08,287 --> 00:08:10,423
but the sound kept getting cut out on both

234
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:11,991
with little difference between them

235
00:08:12,058 --> 00:08:15,194
Finally we put both phones in a box that blocks all signal

236
00:08:15,194 --> 00:08:16,629
waited until they lost connection

237
00:08:16,729 --> 00:08:18,865
then open it and repeat this ten times

238
00:08:18,998 --> 00:08:20,566
The 18 Pro took 5.2

239
00:08:20,566 --> 00:08:22,335
seconds on average to reconnect

240
00:08:22,368 --> 00:08:24,971
while the 17 Pro just took 1.5 seconds

241
00:08:25,204 --> 00:08:27,473
overall the 17 Pro still did a bit better

242
00:08:27,473 --> 00:08:29,509
than the 18 Pro with Apple's own modem

243
00:08:29,509 --> 00:08:31,110
sitting right next to the C2  is

244
00:08:31,110 --> 00:08:32,912
2nm A20 Pro chip

245
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:34,714
raw performance is monstrous

246
00:08:34,747 --> 00:08:37,550
in Geekbench 6 at a 25 degree room temperature

247
00:08:37,717 --> 00:08:39,552
single core scores broke 4700

248
00:08:40,052 --> 00:08:41,554
a 23% jump

249
00:08:41,888 --> 00:08:44,323
multi-core jumped 20% and GPU gains

250
00:08:44,490 --> 00:08:46,325
approached nearly 50%

251
00:08:46,325 --> 00:08:47,894
A genuine big Leap

252
00:08:47,894 --> 00:08:49,896
Does that translate to real world Gaming

253
00:08:49,896 --> 00:08:52,665
We unlocked the 1080P mode in death stranding

254
00:08:52,665 --> 00:08:55,268
the 18 Pro Max managed to hit 40 fps

255
00:08:55,268 --> 00:08:58,671
a full 10 fps higher than the previous generation

256
00:08:58,671 --> 00:08:59,705
shifting experience

257
00:08:59,705 --> 00:09:01,474
to something reasonably playable

258
00:09:01,574 --> 00:09:04,377
Estimated package power peaked at 6.3 Watts

259
00:09:04,410 --> 00:09:05,478
Withdraw that high

260
00:09:05,478 --> 00:09:07,280
can the thermals actually keep up

261
00:09:07,513 --> 00:09:08,948
Surprisingly, yes

262
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:10,182
From start to finish

263
00:09:10,182 --> 00:09:14,220
the 18 Pro Max pinned its 45 fps ceiling without throttling

264
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:16,923
The 17 Pro Max started dropping frames just

265
00:09:16,923 --> 00:09:19,425
7 minutes in as its big core throttled back

266
00:09:19,492 --> 00:09:21,394
a sign of heat saturation

267
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:22,395
In earlier iPhones

268
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:24,196
the processor and RAM chips were

269
00:09:24,196 --> 00:09:25,731
stacked right on top of each other

270
00:09:25,798 --> 00:09:27,633
sandwiching two major heat sources

271
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:29,035
On the 18 Pro series

272
00:09:29,035 --> 00:09:31,437
the memory is laid out beside the A20 Pro

273
00:09:31,437 --> 00:09:33,139
lowering concentrated thermal density

274
00:09:33,205 --> 00:09:34,140
on top of that

275
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:35,942
the vapor chamber is 3 times

276
00:09:35,942 --> 00:09:37,610
more larger than the 17 Pro

277
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:40,212
that dual upgrade gives the cooling a massive lift

278
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,515
recording 4K 120 fps

279
00:09:42,515 --> 00:09:43,716
video for 30 minutes

280
00:09:43,816 --> 00:09:45,985
the 16 Pro Max hit 43 degrees

281
00:09:46,118 --> 00:09:48,621
the 17 Pro Max hit 41.3 degrees

282
00:09:48,788 --> 00:09:51,490
and the 18 Pro Max stayed under 40 degrees

283
00:09:51,991 --> 00:09:54,293
of course even with shared thermal upgrades

284
00:09:54,393 --> 00:09:56,562
the larger 18 Pro Max still holds an

285
00:09:56,562 --> 00:09:58,397
average over the standard 18 Pro

286
00:09:59,498 --> 00:10:00,633
But in daily use

287
00:10:00,633 --> 00:10:03,235
it's actually very hard to push this phone to their limit

288
00:10:03,569 --> 00:10:04,737
compared to getting more speed

289
00:10:04,804 --> 00:10:07,373
what shapes our experience day to day is

290
00:10:07,373 --> 00:10:08,174
battery

291
00:10:08,174 --> 00:10:11,010
The 18 Pro packs a 4000 mAh battery

292
00:10:11,010 --> 00:10:12,945
a tiny bump over last year

293
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:16,315
real world endurance however is far better than expected

294
00:10:16,315 --> 00:10:17,717
in our heavy drain battery stress

295
00:10:17,717 --> 00:10:19,352
test from a hundred to dead

296
00:10:19,352 --> 00:10:22,188
the 18 Pro lasts 6 hours and 38 minutes

297
00:10:22,188 --> 00:10:24,790
1 hour and 51 minutes longer than 17 Pro

298
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,993
most of the credit goes to the 2nm A20 Pro

299
00:10:27,026 --> 00:10:29,629
and the more efficient LTPO+ display

300
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:32,131
the 18 Pro Max sees an even bigger jump

301
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:35,735
its 5390 mAh cell pushed the run times to

302
00:10:35,735 --> 00:10:38,170
7 hours and 57 minutes

303
00:10:38,170 --> 00:10:40,940
2 hours and 6 minutes longer than the 17 Pro Max

304
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:42,975
We can pretty much leave power banks at home now

305
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:45,544
Charging speeds finally got a long overdue a bump

306
00:10:45,544 --> 00:10:48,481
using Apple's official 40 to 60 Watts dynamic charger

307
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:50,082
peak power hits 52 Watts

308
00:10:50,082 --> 00:10:50,983
in our tests

309
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:53,185
both the 18 Pro and Max went from

310
00:10:53,185 --> 00:10:55,321
0 to 50%  in just 15 minutes

311
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,722
with a full charge clocking in in

312
00:10:56,722 --> 00:10:58,624
69 and 78 minutes

313
00:10:58,624 --> 00:11:00,426
that's genuinely fast for an iPhone

314
00:11:00,426 --> 00:11:02,695
But there's also some bad news this year

315
00:11:02,762 --> 00:11:04,663
Our 1TB iPhone 18 Pro

316
00:11:04,663 --> 00:11:06,465
had its flash storage downgraded

317
00:11:06,465 --> 00:11:08,834
from TLC to QLC

318
00:11:08,834 --> 00:11:10,669
and we expect the 2TB Pro models

319
00:11:10,669 --> 00:11:11,937
to use QLC too

320
00:11:11,937 --> 00:11:13,272
Here’s how it works

321
00:11:13,272 --> 00:11:15,708
flash storage is made up of huge numbers

322
00:11:15,708 --> 00:11:17,576
of floating-gate transistors

323
00:11:17,576 --> 00:11:18,377
To store data

324
00:11:18,377 --> 00:11:20,246
we put electrons in these gates

325
00:11:20,246 --> 00:11:21,047
and to read it

326
00:11:21,047 --> 00:11:23,449
we check how many electrons are inside

327
00:11:23,449 --> 00:11:25,951
TLC stores 3 bits in each gate

328
00:11:25,951 --> 00:11:28,888
using 8 states based on the number of electrons

329
00:11:28,888 --> 00:11:31,390
QLC stores 4 bits in each gate

330
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:32,558
with 16 states

331
00:11:32,558 --> 00:11:34,727
This lets the same gate hold more data

332
00:11:34,727 --> 00:11:35,828
bringing costs down

333
00:11:35,828 --> 00:11:36,896
But with more gates

334
00:11:36,896 --> 00:11:39,031
reading and writing need to be more precise

335
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:41,100
which shortens the life of the flash storage

336
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:41,834
But luckily

337
00:11:41,834 --> 00:11:43,869
even QLC is enough for us

338
00:11:43,869 --> 00:11:45,838
with writing 100 GB a day

339
00:11:45,838 --> 00:11:47,206
for ten years straight

340
00:11:47,206 --> 00:11:48,541
still wouldn’t wear it out

341
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:49,942
If it bothers you

342
00:11:49,942 --> 00:11:51,377
pick the lower storage model

343
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:52,878
which still use TLC

344
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:54,046
That’s it for the hardware

345
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:54,714
now let’s see

346
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:56,816
what’s new in this year’s software

347
00:11:56,816 --> 00:11:57,783
On the software side

348
00:11:57,783 --> 00:11:59,585
last year’s Liquid Glass looked nice

349
00:11:59,585 --> 00:12:01,821
but it had plenty of lag and bugs

350
00:12:01,821 --> 00:12:03,155
So with iOS 27

351
00:12:03,155 --> 00:12:04,423
Apple’s main focus is

352
00:12:04,423 --> 00:12:05,257
speed

353
00:12:05,257 --> 00:12:06,625
Even AirDrop is faster

354
00:12:06,625 --> 00:12:07,860
If you use AirDrop a lot

355
00:12:07,860 --> 00:12:09,528
you know it’s been getting worse

356
00:12:09,528 --> 00:12:11,097
so does the new system help?

357
00:12:11,097 --> 00:12:12,431
We tested it in our office

358
00:12:12,431 --> 00:12:14,400
and compared to iOS 26

359
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:17,069
its average speed went up by a whopping…

360
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:18,771
2.4 MB/s

361
00:12:18,771 --> 00:12:21,073
And on both iOS 26 and 27

362
00:12:21,073 --> 00:12:22,241
AirDrop’s average speed

363
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:23,843
stayed below 20 MB/s

364
00:12:23,843 --> 00:12:26,011
so there’s still lots of room to improve

365
00:12:26,011 --> 00:12:26,979
But the good news is

366
00:12:26,979 --> 00:12:28,180
across the system

367
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:30,850
we saw far fewer stutters than 26

368
00:12:30,850 --> 00:12:32,885
so if you held off because you feared lag

369
00:12:32,885 --> 00:12:35,454
you can now go ahead and update to 27

370
00:12:35,454 --> 00:12:36,722
But at what cost?

371
00:12:36,722 --> 00:12:37,790
If you care about design

372
00:12:37,790 --> 00:12:38,691
you’ll notice

373
00:12:38,691 --> 00:12:40,326
Liquid Glass in iOS 27

374
00:12:40,326 --> 00:12:42,294
has been seriously toned down

375
00:12:42,294 --> 00:12:43,462
The highlights that moved

376
00:12:43,462 --> 00:12:44,597
as you tilted your phone

377
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:45,464
now stay still

378
00:12:45,464 --> 00:12:48,100
The light scattering around the edges is gone

379
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:50,169
and the glass looks less clear than before

380
00:12:50,169 --> 00:12:51,070
On dark screens

381
00:12:51,070 --> 00:12:53,239
the glass used to adjust transparency

382
00:12:53,239 --> 00:12:54,440
to match the background

383
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,474
But in the new system

384
00:12:55,474 --> 00:12:56,809
no matter how you scroll

385
00:12:56,809 --> 00:12:58,611
the glass stays the same color

386
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:00,579
There’s a slider in settings to adjust it

387
00:13:00,579 --> 00:13:02,248
but you can't get the feel back

388
00:13:02,248 --> 00:13:04,016
like my hair after I told the barber

389
00:13:04,016 --> 00:13:04,884
Just a trim

390
00:13:04,884 --> 00:13:05,818
Beyond the speed boosts

391
00:13:05,818 --> 00:13:07,052
and small design changes

392
00:13:07,052 --> 00:13:09,021
the biggest update this is AI

393
00:13:09,021 --> 00:13:11,056
The Photos app now lets you expand an image

394
00:13:11,056 --> 00:13:12,358
giving it a wider view

395
00:13:12,358 --> 00:13:14,026
I tried it ten times in a row

396
00:13:14,026 --> 00:13:15,861
and it felt like falling into a wormhole

397
00:13:15,861 --> 00:13:16,796
But the most fun feature

398
00:13:16,796 --> 00:13:18,130
is this spatial reframing

399
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,565
It lets you change the camera angle

400
00:13:19,565 --> 00:13:20,766
after taking a photo

401
00:13:20,766 --> 00:13:21,901
So if I keep turning

402
00:13:21,901 --> 00:13:23,035
can I see my own back?

403
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:26,472
You can

404
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:28,707
but it looks like you’ve turned into another world

405
00:13:28,707 --> 00:13:30,242
if you don’t want to shoot anything at all

406
00:13:30,242 --> 00:13:32,044
there’s a built-in AI image app 

407
00:13:32,044 --> 00:13:33,279
Image Playground

408
00:13:33,279 --> 00:13:34,613
but the images it makes

409
00:13:34,613 --> 00:13:37,249
let’s just say they’re still stuck in 2023

410
00:13:37,249 --> 00:13:38,884
The old Siri wasn’t too bright

411
00:13:38,884 --> 00:13:40,386
when you asked it to do something

412
00:13:40,386 --> 00:13:41,921
it just hand you a web page

413
00:13:41,921 --> 00:13:44,290
The second-generation added the glow around the screen

414
00:13:44,290 --> 00:13:45,724
But only went from five-year-old

415
00:13:45,724 --> 00:13:46,859
to eight-year-old

416
00:13:46,859 --> 00:13:47,526
And now

417
00:13:47,526 --> 00:13:49,061
Siri has turned into a glass orb

418
00:13:49,061 --> 00:13:50,429
living inside the Island

419
00:13:50,429 --> 00:13:52,198
You can pull it up from any interface

420
00:13:52,198 --> 00:13:54,633
and have a conversation with it using text

421
00:13:54,633 --> 00:13:56,101
So how capable is it?

422
00:13:56,101 --> 00:13:58,437
Can it replace those AI apps on your phone?

423
00:13:58,437 --> 00:14:00,072
I brought in ChatGPT and Gemini

424
00:14:00,072 --> 00:14:01,674
to see how they respond

425
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:04,310
The car wash is only 50 meters from my home

426
00:14:04,310 --> 00:14:05,978
Should I drive or walk?

427
00:14:05,978 --> 00:14:08,848
GPT and Gemini both spotted the logical trap

428
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:11,317
only Siri told me to walk to the car wash

429
00:14:11,317 --> 00:14:12,051
Next one

430
00:14:12,051 --> 00:14:13,285
I just learned my parents

431
00:14:13,285 --> 00:14:15,087
didn't invite me to their wedding

432
00:14:15,087 --> 00:14:16,021
I'm really upset

433
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:16,956
What should I do?

434
00:14:16,956 --> 00:14:18,924
They're all pretty good at comforting me

435
00:14:18,924 --> 00:14:20,192
but I wasn't even born

436
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:21,660
when my parents got married

437
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:22,394
And finally

438
00:14:22,394 --> 00:14:23,495
a math problem

439
00:14:23,495 --> 00:14:25,598
Can a 6-meter pole fit through a door?

440
00:14:25,598 --> 00:14:28,000
4 meters high and 3 meters wide?

441
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,169
ChatGPT and Gemini both got the right answer

442
00:14:30,169 --> 00:14:32,271
while Siri gave us 5

443
00:14:32,271 --> 00:14:33,606
But Siri isn't just about having

444
00:14:33,606 --> 00:14:35,241
conversation head anymore

445
00:14:35,241 --> 00:14:36,242
like other AI

446
00:14:36,242 --> 00:14:38,477
It now has a dedicated app of its own

447
00:14:38,477 --> 00:14:39,612
where you can save history

448
00:14:39,612 --> 00:14:41,914
and access it across your Mac and iPad

449
00:14:43,616 --> 00:14:44,049
So

450
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:45,417
 if you use it just to chat

451
00:14:45,417 --> 00:14:47,253
it may still in 2024

452
00:14:47,253 --> 00:14:49,121
But as an AI built into the system

453
00:14:49,121 --> 00:14:50,489
it can do things others can’t

454
00:14:50,889 --> 00:14:51,724
For example

455
00:14:52,524 --> 00:14:53,092
Siri

456
00:14:53,092 --> 00:14:54,526
Check my latest flyght itinerary

457
00:14:54,526 --> 00:14:55,961
text a friend who's picking me

458
00:14:55,961 --> 00:14:57,529
up with my arrival time and terminal

459
00:14:57,529 --> 00:14:58,364
add my first meeting

460
00:14:58,364 --> 00:14:59,832
after I land to my calendar

461
00:14:59,832 --> 00:15:00,532
and remind me

462
00:15:00,532 --> 00:15:02,167
to bring my passport before I head out

463
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,608
That command took a while

464
00:15:09,608 --> 00:15:11,377
but it worked across five apps

465
00:15:11,377 --> 00:15:12,778
and got those done for me

466
00:15:12,778 --> 00:15:14,513
This where Siri really shines

467
00:15:14,513 --> 00:15:15,981
It knows my personal details

468
00:15:15,981 --> 00:15:17,016
can use apps

469
00:15:17,016 --> 00:15:19,051
and truly be my personal assistant

470
00:15:19,051 --> 00:15:20,419
But now it only works

471
00:15:20,419 --> 00:15:21,654
within Apple's own apps

472
00:15:21,654 --> 00:15:22,922
Apple has opened up Siri

473
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:24,323
to third-party apps

474
00:15:24,323 --> 00:15:25,758
but whether developers

475
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:27,126
want to share data with Siri

476
00:15:27,126 --> 00:15:28,394
that’s another story

477
00:15:28,394 --> 00:15:30,796
At the end of last year’s iPhone 17 video

478
00:15:30,796 --> 00:15:31,931
we made a little skit

479
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:34,066
showing the AI assistant we dreamed of

480
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:35,634
Siri

481
00:15:35,634 --> 00:15:37,202
got a lot smarter this year

482
00:15:37,202 --> 00:15:39,071
it's still pretty far from the AI system

483
00:15:39,071 --> 00:15:40,239
 you've been dreaming of

484
00:15:40,239 --> 00:15:42,007
which brings me to a bigger problem

485
00:15:42,007 --> 00:15:44,443
Does AI actually matter to Apple

486
00:15:44,443 --> 00:15:45,811
Since ChatGPT came out

487
00:15:45,811 --> 00:15:46,812
Apple's own models haven't

488
00:15:46,812 --> 00:15:48,580
appeared on any leaderboards

489
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:50,082
It hasn't made a big investment

490
00:15:50,082 --> 00:15:51,450
 on leading AI companies

491
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:52,985
Its AI spending doesn't even get a

492
00:15:52,985 --> 00:15:54,954
separate line in its reports

493
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:55,721
Meanwhile

494
00:15:55,721 --> 00:15:57,489
Google,  Microsoft and Amazon

495
00:15:57,489 --> 00:15:59,692
each spent nearly $100 billion

496
00:15:59,692 --> 00:16:02,161
Whether by choice or because it had no choice

497
00:16:02,161 --> 00:16:03,996
Apple has been moving very slowly

498
00:16:03,996 --> 00:16:05,864
but it's okay to be slow

499
00:16:05,864 --> 00:16:06,665
For three years

500
00:16:06,665 --> 00:16:08,367
 iPhone sold in Mainland China

501
00:16:08,367 --> 00:16:10,069
had no Apple intelligence 

502
00:16:10,069 --> 00:16:11,303
Yet Apple's market share

503
00:16:11,303 --> 00:16:12,805
has grown rather than fallen

504
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:14,473
It turns out few users care about

505
00:16:14,473 --> 00:16:16,542
built-in AI as long as they can install

506
00:16:16,542 --> 00:16:17,910
their choice of AI apps

507
00:16:17,910 --> 00:16:19,945
And whichever model wins in the end

508
00:16:19,945 --> 00:16:21,780
 it still needs a screen to reach the user

509
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:23,916
Apple has a billion of those screens

510
00:16:23,916 --> 00:16:25,484
It doesn't need to build the best model

511
00:16:25,484 --> 00:16:27,386
to have a strong place in this new era

512
00:16:27,386 --> 00:16:28,354
But this year

513
00:16:28,354 --> 00:16:29,688
 AI still hit Apple

514
00:16:29,688 --> 00:16:30,322
In a way

515
00:16:30,322 --> 00:16:31,490
 everyone can feel

516
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,725
higher prices

517
00:16:32,725 --> 00:16:34,660
From the first iPhone to iPhone 17

518
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:35,461
starting price

519
00:16:35,461 --> 00:16:37,963
slowly rose from $499 to $799

520
00:16:37,963 --> 00:16:40,165
raising 2.65% a year

521
00:16:40,165 --> 00:16:41,433
close to the 3%

522
00:16:41,433 --> 00:16:42,601
yearly growth income

523
00:16:42,601 --> 00:16:44,436
But this year that balance broke

524
00:16:44,436 --> 00:16:46,939
Tech giants are rushing to build data centers

525
00:16:46,939 --> 00:16:48,640
driving up the cost of parts

526
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:50,709
Samsung,  SKHynix and Micron

527
00:16:50,709 --> 00:16:52,511
faced major memory shortages

528
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:54,346
Even supply chain expert Tim Cook

529
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:56,081
in his 40-year career says he's

530
00:16:56,081 --> 00:16:57,816
never seen anything like it

531
00:16:57,816 --> 00:16:59,985
To cope Apple delayed the base iPhone 18

532
00:16:59,985 --> 00:17:01,153
onto the next spring

533
00:17:01,153 --> 00:17:03,355
saving limited memory for the pricier Pro

534
00:17:03,355 --> 00:17:04,456
and Duo models

535
00:17:04,456 --> 00:17:06,658
and cutting costs wherever possible

536
00:17:06,658 --> 00:17:09,595
bringing screens from $110 down to $70

537
00:17:09,595 --> 00:17:10,362
and downgrading larger

538
00:17:10,362 --> 00:17:12,831
storage options from TLC to QLC

539
00:17:12,831 --> 00:17:13,599
But even then

540
00:17:13,599 --> 00:17:15,734
the 1TB iPhone 18 Pro Max cost

541
00:17:15,734 --> 00:17:17,469
compared with last year's model

542
00:17:17,469 --> 00:17:19,638
nearly $300 more to make

543
00:17:19,638 --> 00:17:20,806
So in the US

544
00:17:20,806 --> 00:17:23,108
the 18 Pro now starts at $100 higher

545
00:17:23,108 --> 00:17:24,576
and the top 2TB model

546
00:17:24,576 --> 00:17:26,779
is up at a full $500

547
00:17:26,779 --> 00:17:28,547
And this is just the start

548
00:17:28,547 --> 00:17:29,581
In 2027

549
00:17:29,581 --> 00:17:32,284
memory and storage prices are set to rise again

550
00:17:32,284 --> 00:17:33,852
taking up nearly half of the phone's

551
00:17:33,852 --> 00:17:35,054
total parts cost

552
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,056
making iPhones even more expensive 

553
00:17:37,523 --> 00:17:39,691
Apple may be able to watch the AI revolution

554
00:17:39,691 --> 00:17:40,859
from the sidelines

555
00:17:40,859 --> 00:17:42,327
but it can't escape its impact

556
00:17:42,828 --> 00:17:44,196
Every time I think about this

557
00:17:44,196 --> 00:17:45,964
 I feel a little uneasy

558
00:17:45,964 --> 00:17:48,567
If even a company as big as Apple

559
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:50,436
can't stay out of the harm's way

560
00:17:50,436 --> 00:17:51,503
What about us?

561
00:17:51,503 --> 00:17:53,906
AI changing our lives is no longer a prediction

562
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:55,974
but a fast moving reality

563
00:17:55,974 --> 00:17:57,476
Coding agents have changed the way

564
00:17:57,476 --> 00:17:59,077
we write code completely

565
00:17:59,077 --> 00:18:00,145
AI videos are almost

566
00:18:00,145 --> 00:18:02,281
impossible to tell from the real ones

567
00:18:02,281 --> 00:18:03,782
Reinforcement learning lets robots

568
00:18:03,782 --> 00:18:05,517
improve at record speed

569
00:18:05,517 --> 00:18:06,251
Every two months

570
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:08,086
a new model transforms an industry

571
00:18:08,086 --> 00:18:10,255
and skills took years to learn yesterday

572
00:18:10,255 --> 00:18:12,257
may need just one prompt tomorrow 

573
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:13,325
So while making this video

574
00:18:13,325 --> 00:18:14,993
I often feel a bit lost

575
00:18:14,993 --> 00:18:16,428
We used to review the new iPhones

576
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:17,229
and call Apple's launch

577
00:18:17,229 --> 00:18:18,897
the biggest show in tech

578
00:18:18,897 --> 00:18:20,032
because it was the most advanced

579
00:18:20,032 --> 00:18:21,633
technology that most people

580
00:18:21,633 --> 00:18:23,001
could actually get their hands on

581
00:18:23,001 --> 00:18:24,103
Every small change showed

582
00:18:24,103 --> 00:18:25,671
us where tech was going

583
00:18:25,671 --> 00:18:27,506
Today,  we still review new iPhones

584
00:18:27,506 --> 00:18:29,241
comparing two photos up close

585
00:18:29,241 --> 00:18:31,076
checking how much faster the chip is

586
00:18:31,076 --> 00:18:32,544
just like 10 years ago

587
00:18:32,544 --> 00:18:33,979
But times have changed

588
00:18:33,979 --> 00:18:36,281
the iPhone is no longer the center of tech

589
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:37,516
and the world outside

590
00:18:37,516 --> 00:18:39,017
moves at a different speed

591
00:18:39,017 --> 00:18:41,854
That speed blows a maze and scares us

592
00:18:41,854 --> 00:18:43,255
How can we keep up with this world?

593
00:18:43,255 --> 00:18:44,022
Will the future

594
00:18:44,022 --> 00:18:45,457
still have a place for us

595
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:47,292
In a parody video a decade ago

596
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:50,062
the iPhone 18 was an absurdly long stick

597
00:18:50,062 --> 00:18:51,163
which was a joke

598
00:18:51,163 --> 00:18:52,064
but it also showed

599
00:18:52,064 --> 00:18:53,966
how it makes sense of the world

600
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:56,168
The iPhone 5 was longer than the 4

601
00:18:56,168 --> 00:18:57,135
so by linear logic

602
00:18:57,135 --> 00:18:58,837
the 18 Pro should be this long

603
00:18:58,837 --> 00:19:01,273
But now the iPhone 18 is here

604
00:19:01,273 --> 00:19:03,609
It's still a screen we hold in our hand

605
00:19:03,609 --> 00:19:05,377
While the world outside the screen

606
00:19:05,377 --> 00:19:08,413
has moved far beyond simple linear logic 

607
00:19:08,413 --> 00:19:09,648
growing and racing

608
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:11,383
in ways we can't imagine

609
00:19:11,383 --> 00:19:13,752
But no matter how powerful AI gets

610
00:19:13,752 --> 00:19:15,420
there's still one thing it can't do

611
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:16,622
generate a single shot

612
00:19:16,622 --> 00:19:18,056
longer than 30 seconds

613
00:19:18,056 --> 00:19:18,690
That's right

614
00:19:18,690 --> 00:19:20,459
even the best video models today 

615
00:19:20,459 --> 00:19:21,426
can only generate

616
00:19:21,426 --> 00:19:23,195
30 seconds in one shot

617
00:19:23,195 --> 00:19:24,029
So in this video

618
00:19:24,029 --> 00:19:25,264
we decided to try

619
00:19:25,264 --> 00:19:26,832
one continuous shot

620
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:28,200
It was a painful process

621
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:30,002
we messed up countless times

622
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,403
did countless retakes

623
00:19:31,403 --> 00:19:33,105
and there are hidden cuts in between

624
00:19:33,105 --> 00:19:35,274
So it is really more of a fake one take

625
00:19:35,274 --> 00:19:36,141
But in the end

626
00:19:36,141 --> 00:19:36,808
we managed 

627
00:19:36,808 --> 00:19:38,010
to fade the 18 Pro part

628
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,778
into one unbroken shot

629
00:19:39,778 --> 00:19:40,512
It's a small act of

630
00:19:40,512 --> 00:19:42,681
stubbornness in the age of AI

631
00:19:42,681 --> 00:19:43,815
But more importantly

632
00:19:43,815 --> 00:19:44,983
we wanted to put in the effort

633
00:19:44,983 --> 00:19:46,418
 to give you something different

634
00:19:46,418 --> 00:19:47,553
Time was tight

635
00:19:47,553 --> 00:19:48,854
there were plenty of flaws

636
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:50,589
 but we hope you enjoy it

637
00:19:50,589 --> 00:19:52,491
Saying this won't change anything

638
00:19:52,491 --> 00:19:54,159
but sometime I really feel that

639
00:19:54,159 --> 00:19:55,661
 keeping up with this world

640
00:19:55,661 --> 00:19:56,995
is so tiring

641
00:19:56,995 --> 00:19:58,130
Sometimes I really wish

642
00:19:58,130 --> 00:19:59,731
the world were linear

643
00:19:59,731 --> 00:20:01,533
and sometimes I really miss the days

644
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:02,701
when we could hold the future

645
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:03,569
in our hands

646
00:20:07,005 --> 00:20:07,639
Ok guys

647
00:20:07,639 --> 00:20:08,807
that's it for this video

648
00:20:08,807 --> 00:20:09,808
It's another year and

649
00:20:09,808 --> 00:20:10,876
another iPhone review

650
00:20:11,109 --> 00:20:11,810
If you liked it

651
00:20:11,810 --> 00:20:12,711
please give us a like

652
00:20:12,844 --> 00:20:13,579
Thank you so much for

653
00:20:13,579 --> 00:20:14,313
watching till the end

654
00:20:14,513 --> 00:20:15,180
See you next time

